        "original_id": "cc88aed1-6364-55c6-bce8-f3b93bdbbbd6",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Dick Bremer, Bert Blyleven, Jack Morris, Roy Smalley III, Torii Hunter, Michael Cuddyer, LaTroy Hawkins, Scott Ullger\n- Organizations: Minnesota Twins, Detroit Tigers, Major League Baseball\n- Roles: Television broadcasters, starting pitcher\n\nFacts:\n- Jack Morris was born on May 16, 1955.\n- Jack Morris is an American former professional baseball starting pitcher who played in Major League Baseball from 1977 to 1994.\n- Jack Morris played mainly for the Detroit Tigers and won 254 games during his career.\n- Dick Bremer works on Minnesota Twins television broadcasts with Bert Blyleven for home games.\n- Dick Bremer works on Minnesota Twins television broadcasts with Jack Morris, Roy Smalley III, Torii Hunter, Michael Cuddyer, or LaTroy Hawkins for road games.\n- Bert Blyleven and Dick Bremer frequently referred to Scott Ullger as \"Scotty,\" and Minnesota Twins fans also used that nickname.",
